<p>This page explains what information WhereIsTheBin uses and why. We try to use as little as the service needs. We do not show advertising, we do not currently use analytics or tracking tools, and we do not sell personal information.</p>

<h2>Browsing without an account</h2>
<p>You can use the map and place pages without an account, and we do not ask you for personal information. Like most websites, our server keeps basic technical logs (for example your IP address, the time and the page requested) to keep the service running and secure. Search words and coordinates that appear in the web address are not written to these logs. Our hosting provider may also keep its own logs.</p>

<h2>Your location</h2>
<p>We only ask your browser for your location when you press a button such as "Use my location" or "Walking directions", and your browser asks for your permission first. We do not store your location or build a history of where you have been.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Nearby places.</strong> Your coordinates are sent to our server to find nearby places, and are not saved.</li>
  <li><strong>Walking directions.</strong> Your position and the destination are sent through our server to a free public routing service run by FOSSGIS (OpenStreetMap Germany). That service says it keeps server logs of requests. While you follow directions, your device tracks your position to show the next turn; your position is sent again only if you leave the route and a new route is needed.</li>
  <li><strong>Place search.</strong> The words you type are sent through our server to Nominatim, the search service of OpenStreetMap.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Accounts</h2>
<p>If you create an account we keep your name, your email address and a one-way scrambled form (a hash) of your password, so we cannot read your password. We also keep your language choice. We need this to let you add places, send reports and see your contributions. Moderators can see the name of the person who submitted a place or report.</p>

<h2>What you contribute</h2>
<p>Places, notes and reports you send are linked to your account so moderators can review them and you can follow their status. A published place shows information about the place only; it does not show who added it. Reports are not public. When moderators act on a place or report, the action and the moderator's name are recorded in an audit log.</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>We use two small cookies, both needed for the site to work:</p>
<ul>
  <li>a session cookie that keeps you logged in and protects forms from misuse; it expires after 14 days;</li>
  <li>a language cookie that remembers whether you chose English or Malayalam; it lasts one year.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not use cookies for advertising or tracking.</p>

<h2>Other services that see your visit</h2>
<p>Map pictures are loaded from OpenStreetMap's servers and text fonts from Google Fonts. As with any website you visit, these services can see your IP address and basic device details. We do not send them your name, email or contributions.</p>

<h2>Keeping and deleting data</h2>
<p>We keep your account and contributions while you use the service. You can ask us to correct or delete your account data using the contact address below. We will tell you what we can remove; places that have already been published for everyone may need to stay on the map.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If we change how we use information, we will update this page and its date.</p>